Emerging Healthcare Trends Reinforcing Market Growth
The rising global burden of cerebrovascular disease continues to reshape treatment priorities. According to the World Health Organization, stroke remains one of the leading causes of disability and death worldwide — a trend accelerating demand for fast-acting injectable therapies that support cerebral blood flow and reduce ischemic damage.
Three emerging shifts are shaping the market trajectory:
•	Increasing clinical adoption of precision-driven acute stroke protocols
•	Growing prioritization of hospital-based neurovascular care infrastructure
•	Shifting reimbursement and procurement models supporting injectable therapies for critical care
These dynamics reflect growing awareness, evolving medical guidelines, and a broader transition toward advanced neurological intervention models.
